      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find out how many nickels Jamie has, let's denote the number of each type of coin as \\( n \\). The value of the nickels is \\( 0.05n \\) dollars, the value of the dimes is \\( 0.10n \\) dollars, and the value of the quarters is \\( 0.25n \\) dollars. The total value of all the coins is given as $13.20.\n\nWe can set up the equation for the total value as follows:\n\\[\n0.05n + 0.10n + 0.25n = 13.20\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine the terms on the left side of the equation:\n\\[\n0.05n + 0.10n + 0.25n = 0.40n\n\\]\n\nSo the equation simplifies to:\n\\[\n0.40n = 13.20\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( n \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 0.40:\n\\[\nn = \\frac{13.20}{0.40} = 33\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Jamie has \\(\\boxed{33}\\) nickels.",
